Presidential elections were held in [[Cyprus]] on 8 February 1998, with a second round on 15 February.<ref name=NS>[[Dieter Nohlen]] & Philip Stöver (2010) ''Elections in Europe: A data handbook'', p438 {{ISBN|978-3-8329-5609-7}}</ref> The result was a victory for [[Glafcos Clerides]] of the [[Democratic Rally]] after he finished as runner-up behind [[Georgios Iacovou]] (who was supported by [[Progressive Party of Working People|AKEL]] and the [[Democratic Party (Cyprus)|Democratic Party]])<ref name=N2>Nohlen & Stöver, p447</ref> in the first round. Voter turnout was 92% in the first round and 93% in the second.<ref name=N2/>

